# Nougat extraction stub

**Status:** Not run. Not needed for this paper.

## Why this is a stub

The source PDF (`source/paper.pdf`, Guerra Liberal et al., Sci Rep 13:11198, 2023) has a **clean embedded text layer**. `pdftotext` (poppler) extracted the full main-text body, all equation labels, and all figure captions without OCR errors --- see `ocr/paper.txt`.

Under the LUCID pipeline's "run nougat only when the text layer is missing or garbled" rule, this paper did not qualify. Running nougat here would consume ~1 GPU-minute on uicgpu to produce a marginally-different Markdown rendering of the same text that pdftotext already gave us cleanly.

The SI PDF (`source/SI_MOESM1_ESM.pdf`, Table S1) was also successfully processed by `pdftotext` --- see `source/SI_MOESM1_ESM.txt`. The SI XLSX (`source/SI_MOESM2_ESM.xlsx`) is the real quantitative payload; it is a native spreadsheet with three data-tabs (Fig 1, Fig 2, Fig 3 raw data), converted to CSVs by `code/extract_si.py` without any OCR step.

## If a future backfill wants a real nougat pass

Free-endpoint recipe on uicgpu:
```
conda activate nougat
nougat source/paper.pdf -o extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base
```
Output would land at `extraction/paper.mmd` (Markdown + math). Estimated ~1 min on one A100. Not required for the current REPLICATED verdict.

## What is in this stub file
Nothing extractive. This file exists only to satisfy the 8-artifact backfill checklist and to document the deliberate decision not to run nougat on a text-layer-clean PDF.
